---
import SiteLayout from '../../layouts/SiteLayout.astro'
import '../../styles/frontier.css'
import { currentFrontier, frontierProgressSnapshots, frontierReleases, frontierRegistry } from '../../lib/frontier'

const serializedReleases = JSON.stringify(frontierReleases).replaceAll('<', '\\u003c')
const serializedSnapshots = JSON.stringify(frontierProgressSnapshots).replaceAll('<', '\\u003c')
const statusLabels = { established: 'Established', partial: 'Partial', open: 'Open', falsified: 'Falsified', not_applicable: 'Not applicable' }
const partialLabels = { typed_not_constructed: 'Typed, not constructed', constructed_not_verified: 'Constructed, not verified', verified_limited_scope: 'Verified in limited scope', blocked_missing_source_input: 'Blocked by missing source input' }
---

<SiteLayout
  title="Frontier Atlas · Marici"
  description="Versioned cross-sector research frontiers, pinned to the ledger, epistemic graph, and Git history."
>
  <section class="atlas-page" aria-labelledby="atlas-title">
    <header class="atlas-hero">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Standing cross-sector synthesis</p>
        <h1 id="atlas-title">Frontier Atlas</h1>
        <p class="lede">Immutable snapshots of what is established, what remains missing, and which comparison arrow each sector is testing.</p>
      </div>
      <aside class="atlas-current" aria-label="Current frontier release">
        <span>Current release</span>
        <strong>v{currentFrontier.version}</strong>
        <p>{currentFrontier.label}</p>
      </aside>
    </header>

    <nav class="observatory-boundary" aria-label="Related versioned research views">
      <span>Frontier Atlas: what comes next</span>
      <a href="/oddballs/">Oddball Observatory: what refuses to disappear →</a>
    </nav>

    <section class="release-changes" aria-labelledby="live-rh-frontier">
      <p class="eyebrow">Live working frontier · not a rewritten release</p>
      <h2 id="live-rh-frontier">RH: the source germ is rigid; zero confinement remains open</h2>
      <p>
        The current carrier is a target-relative marked germ, quotiented by complete target fibers and
        congruence-closed under every admitted source constructor. The full arithmetic module is a presentation;
        it survives in the germ only where an authorized constructor orbit can make its distinctions observable.
      </p>
      <div class="sector-grid" aria-label="Live RH frontier summary">
        <article class="sector-card">
          <header><div><p>Established</p><h3>Canonical source section</h3></div><span>Exact</span></header>
          <div class="sector-result">
            <strong>Sharp result</strong>
            <p>Euler–theta overlap rejects a reciprocal-even hostile divisor multiplier in the zero-free Euler chamber before its inserted zeros are inspected.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="sector-frontier">
            <strong>Meaning</strong>
            <p>The completed section is rigidly tied to its labelled source. Arbitrary divisor insertion is not a source-preserving presentation change.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="sector-card">
          <header><div><p>Established obstruction</p><h3>Rotor completion</h3></div><span>No-go</span></header>
          <div class="sector-result">
            <strong>Sharp result</strong>
            <p>Finite nonzero complex rotor–dilation factors can converge to zero. Reciprocal pairing can hide that collapse by coupling it to a divergent inverse sector.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="sector-frontier">
            <strong>Meaning</strong>
            <p>Phase coherence, reciprocal symmetry, and finite invertibility do not protect the completed conformal scale.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="sector-card">
          <header><div><p>Typing correction</p><h3>No time variable is designated</h3></div><span>Full-fiber gate</span></header>
          <div class="sector-result">
            <strong>Sharp result</strong>
            <p>Spectral paths, cutoff refinements, constructor compositions, and chain degrees are distinct index types. None currently carries an authorized temporal interpretation.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="sector-frontier">
            <strong>Admission rule</strong>
            <p>A proposed temporal realization is admissible on the existing germ exactly when it is constant on every complete germ fiber; otherwise the germ must refine.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="sector-card">
          <header><div><p>Open theorem</p><h3>Source-derived scale law</h3></div><span>RH-bearing</span></header>
          <div class="sector-result">
            <strong>Current boundary</strong>
            <p>The labelled source has an invertible spectral comparison, but its fixed scalar augmentation is not horizontal and can cancel between nonzero reciprocal modes.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="sector-next">
            <strong>Next exact test</strong>
            <p>Construct the determinant connection from the constructor-closed marked germ and prove a compact-uniform lower bound on its real path integrals in each open half-plane, without dividing by the completed section.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
      <p class="selector-note">
        Present verdict: provenance is explained; RH is not. The missing mechanism is completion-stable noncollapse of the actual source-derived determinant readout.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="atlas-controls" aria-label="Frontier version controls">
      <label>
        Explore version
        <select id="frontier-version">
          {frontierReleases.map((release) => (
            <option value={release.version} selected={release.version === frontierRegistry.current}>
              v{release.version} · {release.label}
            </option>
          ))}
        </select>
      </label>
      <label>
        Compare against
        <select id="frontier-compare">
          <option value="">No comparison</option>
          {frontierReleases.map((release) => (
            <option value={release.version} selected={release.version === currentFrontier.supersedes}>
              v{release.version} · {release.label}
            </option>
          ))}
        </select>
      </label>
      <button id="frontier-copy-link" type="button">Copy version link</button>
    </section>

    <p id="frontier-live-status" class="sr-only" aria-live="polite"></p>

    {frontierReleases.map((release) => (
      <article
        class="atlas-version"
        data-frontier-version={release.version}
        hidden={release.version !== frontierRegistry.current}
      >
        <header class="release-header">
          <div>
            <p class="release-version">Release v{release.version} · {release.status}</p>
            <h2>{release.label}</h2>
            <p>{release.summary}</p>
          </div>
          <dl class="release-pins">
            <div><dt>Released</dt><dd>{new Date(release.released_at).toLocaleString('en-US', { dateStyle: 'medium', timeStyle: 'short', timeZone: 'UTC' })} UTC</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Source Git baseline</dt><dd><code>{release.pins.git_commit.slice(0, 12)}</code></dd></div>
            <div><dt>Graph event</dt><dd><code>{release.pins.epistemic_event.split('-')[1]}</code></dd></div>
            <div><dt>Ledger ceiling</dt><dd>{release.pins.ledger_sequence_ceiling}</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </header>

        <section class="release-changes" aria-labelledby={'changes-' + release.version}>
          <h3 id={'changes-' + release.version}>What changed in this release</h3>
          <ul>{release.changes.map((change) => <li>{change}</li>)}</ul>
        </section>

        {frontierProgressSnapshots[release.version] && (() => {
          const snapshot = frontierProgressSnapshots[release.version]
          return (
            <section class="progress-chart" aria-labelledby={'progress-' + release.version}>
              <header class="progress-header">
                <div>
                  <p class="eyebrow">Reviewed epistemic-graph projection</p>
                  <h3 id={'progress-' + release.version}>Cross-sector selection pipeline</h3>
                  <p>{snapshot.introduction}</p>
                  <p class="selector-note">{snapshot.selector_note}</p>
                </div>
                <p class="review-badge"><span aria-hidden="true">✓</span> Operator reviewed · v{snapshot.version}</p>
              </header>

              <div class="progress-legend" aria-label="Progress status legend">
                {Object.entries(statusLabels).map(([status, label]) => <span class={'status status-' + status}><i aria-hidden="true"></i>{label}</span>)}
              </div>

              <div class="progress-matrix" role="table" aria-label={'Cross-sector progress in Frontier ' + snapshot.version}>
                <div class="progress-row progress-head" role="row">
                  <span role="columnheader">Sector</span>
                  {snapshot.stages.map((stage) => <span role="columnheader">{stage.label}</span>)}
                </div>
                {snapshot.sectors.map((sector) => (
                  <div class="progress-row" role="row">
                    <div class="sector-label" role="rowheader"><strong>{sector.name}</strong><span>{sector.lens_family_object}</span></div>
                    {snapshot.stages.map((stage) => {
                      const cell = sector.cells[stage.id]
                      return (
                        <details class={'progress-cell status-' + cell.status} role="cell">
                          <summary aria-label={`${sector.name}, ${stage.label}: ${statusLabels[cell.status]}`}>
                            <span class="mobile-stage">{stage.label}</span>
                            <span class={'status status-' + cell.status}><i aria-hidden="true"></i>{statusLabels[cell.status]}</span>
                            {cell.selector_maturity && <small>{cell.selector_maturity.replaceAll('_', ' ')}</small>}
                          </summary>
                          <div class="evidence-panel">
                            <p>{cell.explanation}</p>
                            {cell.partial_reason && <p><strong>Why partial:</strong> {partialLabels[cell.partial_reason]}</p>}
                            <p><strong>Evidence:</strong> {cell.evidence_summary}</p>
                            <p><strong>What remains:</strong> {cell.what_remains}</p>
                            <dl>
                              <div><dt>Reviewed by</dt><dd>{cell.review_owner}</dd></div>
                              <div><dt>Status changed</dt><dd>Frontier v{cell.changed_in_version}</dd></div>
                            </dl>
                            {cell.status_basis.length ? (
                              <ul class="basis-list">
                                {cell.status_basis.map((basis) => <li>{basis.href ? <a href={basis.href}>{basis.label}</a> : <span>{basis.label} · graph {basis.event_id?.split('-')[1]}</span>}</li>)}
                              </ul>
                            ) : <p class="evidence-gap">No admitted status-basis entity is attached. The review approval does not create missing evidence.</p>}
                          </div>
                        </details>
                      )
                    })}
                  </div>
                ))}
              </div>
            </section>
          )
        })()}

        <section class="sector-grid" aria-label={'Sector frontiers in release ' + release.version}>
          {release.sectors.map((sector) => (
            <article class="sector-card" data-sector-id={sector.id}>
              <header>
                <div>
                  <p>{sector.kind}</p>
                  <h3>{sector.name}</h3>
                </div>
                <span>{sector.strength}</span>
              </header>
              <dl>
                <div><dt>Carrier</dt><dd>{sector.carrier}</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Coefficient object</dt><dd>{sector.coefficient}</dd></div>
                <div><dt>Physical selection</dt><dd>{sector.selection}</dd></div>
              </dl>
              <div class="sector-result"><strong>Sharp result</strong><p>{sector.sharp_result}</p></div>
              <div class="sector-frontier"><strong>Open frontier</strong><p>{sector.frontier}</p></div>
              <div class="sector-next"><strong>Next finite test</strong><p>{sector.next_test}</p></div>
              <footer>
                {sector.evidence.map((item) => <a href={item.href}>{item.label} →</a>)}
              </footer>
            </article>
          ))}
        </section>
      </article>
    ))}

    <section id="frontier-comparison" class="atlas-comparison" hidden aria-labelledby="comparison-title">
      <header>
        <p class="eyebrow">Version comparison</p>
        <h2 id="comparison-title">Changed sector fields</h2>
        <p id="comparison-summary"></p>
      </header>
      <div id="comparison-rows"></div>
    </section>

    <section class="atlas-authority">
      <h2>Authority model</h2>
      <p>The Atlas is an immutable interpretive snapshot. Ledger entries remain the mathematical record; the epistemic graph carries claims and supersession; the Git pin names the source baseline interpreted by the release. Git history separately identifies the commit that introduced the release artifact. A later release never rewrites an earlier one.</p>
    </section>
  </section>

  <script is:inline id="frontier-data" type="application/json" set:html={serializedReleases}></script>
  <script is:inline id="frontier-progress-data" type="application/json" set:html={serializedSnapshots}></script>
  <script is:inline>
    const releases = JSON.parse(document.querySelector('#frontier-data').textContent)
    const progressSnapshots = JSON.parse(document.querySelector('#frontier-progress-data').textContent)
    const versionSelect = document.querySelector('#frontier-version')
    const compareSelect = document.querySelector('#frontier-compare')
    const comparison = document.querySelector('#frontier-comparison')
    const comparisonRows = document.querySelector('#comparison-rows')
    const comparisonSummary = document.querySelector('#comparison-summary')
    const liveStatus = document.querySelector('#frontier-live-status')
    const fields = [
      ['carrier', 'Carrier'],
      ['coefficient', 'Coefficient object'],
      ['selection', 'Physical selection'],
      ['sharp_result', 'Sharp result'],
      ['frontier', 'Open frontier'],
      ['next_test', 'Next finite test'],
      ['strength', 'Evidence strength'],
    ]

    function release(version) {
      return releases.find((item) => item.version === version)
    }

    function selectVersion(version, updateHash = true) {
      if (!release(version)) return
      document.querySelectorAll('[data-frontier-version]').forEach((node) => {
        node.hidden = node.dataset.frontierVersion !== version
      })
      versionSelect.value = version
      if (updateHash) history.replaceState(null, '', '#v' + version)
      liveStatus.textContent = 'Showing Frontier Atlas version ' + version
      renderComparison()
    }

    function renderComparison() {
      const selected = release(versionSelect.value)
      const baseline = release(compareSelect.value)
      comparisonRows.replaceChildren()
      if (!selected || !baseline || selected.version === baseline.version) {
        comparison.hidden = true
        return
      }
      comparison.hidden = false
      comparisonSummary.textContent = 'v' + baseline.version + ' → v' + selected.version
      const selectedProgress = progressSnapshots[selected.version]
      const baselineProgress = progressSnapshots[baseline.version]
      if (selectedProgress && !baselineProgress) comparisonSummary.textContent += ' · selection pipeline introduced'
      if (!selectedProgress && baselineProgress) comparisonSummary.textContent += ' · selection pipeline not present in selected version'
      const sectorIds = [...new Set([...baseline.sectors, ...selected.sectors].map((sector) => sector.id))]
      for (const sectorId of sectorIds) {
        const before = baseline.sectors.find((sector) => sector.id === sectorId)
        const after = selected.sectors.find((sector) => sector.id === sectorId)
        const changed = fields.filter(([key]) => before?.[key] !== after?.[key])
        if (!before || !after || changed.length) {
          const card = document.createElement('article')
          card.className = 'comparison-card'
          const heading = document.createElement('h3')
          heading.textContent = after?.name || before?.name || sectorId
          card.append(heading)
          if (!before || !after) {
            const note = document.createElement('p')
            note.textContent = before ? 'Removed in selected release.' : 'Added in selected release.'
            card.append(note)
          } else {
            for (const [key, label] of changed) {
              const row = document.createElement('div')
              const title = document.createElement('strong')
              const oldText = document.createElement('p')
              const newText = document.createElement('p')
              title.textContent = label
              const beforeLabel = document.createElement('span')
              const afterLabel = document.createElement('span')
              beforeLabel.textContent = 'Before'
              afterLabel.textContent = 'After'
              oldText.append(beforeLabel, ' ' + before[key])
              newText.append(afterLabel, ' ' + after[key])
              row.append(title, oldText, newText)
              card.append(row)
            }
          }
          comparisonRows.append(card)
        }
      }
    }

    versionSelect.addEventListener('change', () => selectVersion(versionSelect.value))
    compareSelect.addEventListener('change', renderComparison)
    document.querySelector('#frontier-copy-link').addEventListener('click', async () => {
      const url = new URL(location.href)
      url.hash = 'v' + versionSelect.value
      await navigator.clipboard.writeText(url.href)
      liveStatus.textContent = 'Copied link for Frontier Atlas version ' + versionSelect.value
    })
    const requested = location.hash.match(/^#v(.+)$/)?.[1]
    selectVersion(release(requested) ? requested : versionSelect.value, false)
    renderComparison()
  </script>
</SiteLayout>
